adership good, but show-off may affect crew cooperation, not open to new ideas affects adaptability. No explicit stress resilience, but anticipation may help. Technical competence maybe good.\n\nWhich is best? Hard. I think D seems balanced: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handles unexpected events, but hot temper is serious for crew cooperation. B has nasty remarks, also serious. C has egocentric, communication difficulty. A has show-off, not open to new ideas. All have issues.\n\nMaybe D is strongest because strengths cover many criteria: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, adaptability? Not open to new ideas is not a concern for D. Hot temper is a concern but maybe manageable. I'd recommend D.\n\nThus my public message: propose Candidate D as current recommendation, note strengths and concerns, compare to others.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate D\"."}
